<article class="env-lemma" id="0G1U">
       
      
      
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0G1U">Lemma <span data-tag="0G1U">15.93.20</span>.</a> Let $I$ be a finitely generated ideal of a ring $A$. Let $K$ be a derived complete object of $D(A)$. If $K \otimes _ A^\mathbf {L} A/I = 0$, then $K = 0$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is a special case of Lemma <a href="/tag/0H83" data-tag="0H83">15.93.19</a> but we'll also give a direct proof. Choose generators $f_1, \ldots , f_ r$ of $I$. Denote $K_ n$ the Koszul complex on $f_1^ n, \ldots , f_ r^ n$ over $A$. Recall that $K_ n$ is bounded and that the cohomology modules of $K_ n$ are annihilated by $f_1^ n, \ldots , f_ r^ n$ and hence by $I^{nr}$. By Lemma <a href="/tag/0G1T" data-tag="0G1T">15.90.8</a> we see that $K \otimes _ A^\mathbf {L} K_ n = 0$. Since $K$ is derived complete by Lemma <a href="/tag/0920" data-tag="0920">15.93.18</a> we have $K = R\mathop{\mathrm{lim}}\nolimits K \otimes _ A^\mathbf {L} K_ n = 0$ as desired. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>